# Direct third-party deps of tools/sandbox/*.py and tools/shader_blob_dump.py
# (stdlib otherwise). The gate reads every third-party import under tools/, so a
# new tool cannot add a fifth package here without naming it.
# Each line carries a floor and a ceiling: a recompile resolves inside the
# series the lock was reviewed against, so it cannot silently jump a series
# under a tool that reaches into the package's internals. The series is the
# last component that is not a patch number: ~=1.25.0 and ~=1.25 both mean 1.25.
# tests/test_sandbox_requirements_sync.py checks every bound against the
# locked version, so a bound and a lock that disagree fail the gate.
# Compile to requirements.txt with hashes:
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes requirements.in -o requirements.txt
dnfile~=0.18.0
# Stale upstream (last release Dec 2022) but stable and complete as a CIL
# disassembler; Mandiant-maintained and still the standard Python option.
dncil~=1.0.2
# 1.25.x only: shader_blob_dump.py calls UnityPy.helpers.CompressionHelper,
# which is not a stable API, so a 1.26+ refactor must not land on a recompile.
UnityPy~=1.25.0
